;; Guest session-restore decision: unpack a sealed packed session word.
;;
;; WHY THIS IS A KOTOBA OBJECT AND NOT A C TABLE
;;
;; C already hit-tests windows (wm-hit) and paints in z-order (mechanism).
;; WHICH front window a sealed boot session restores is a compositor
;; decision (root ADR-2608221625 / ADR-0013 Phase 6 session restore).
;; Hosted `kbb -M:compositor wm` does not count. The named leftover
;; after this object is linked is still `:native-compositor-absent`
;; (native component runtime, P5).
;;
;; ABI: [packed] -> restored front window id, or 0 refuse.
;; Boot packed session is front window 2 (hosted boot-desktop z-front).
;; Vector:
;;   0 -> 0   empty session is leftover :empty-session
;;   1 -> 1   front is window 1
;;   2 -> 2   boot packed session
;;   3 -> 0   unknown surface is leftover :unknown-surface
;; Returning 2 for packed 0 is leftover :always-front.
;; Ignoring the restored front in wm-hit is leftover :restore-ignored.
;;
;; Temporary native constraint: word types only, nested `if`, not a map
;; (ADR-2608650000: an unavailable backend is not a language ceiling).
;; Param name matches ime-romaji (`a`).
;;
;; Not a second compositor west repo. Not hosted JVM WM. Not CACAO write.

(defn aiueos-session-restore [a]
  (if (< a 1) 0
    (if (< a 3) a
      0)))

(defn main [] 0)
